      "question": {
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "- $B$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $6\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $-6\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nB-{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
